# check-public.allow — known, justified exceptions to scripts/check-public.sh.
#
# One entry per line: `path` (suppress every hit in that file) or
# `path:regex` (suppress only hits whose matched line matches regex).
# Comments (#) and blank lines are ignored. Every entry is a KNOWN leak
# pending a tracked cleanup — cite the beads issue (or design-doc rationale)
# next to any new entry. See:
#   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-27-infra-content-separation-design.md

# (The doctor's JOBS list moved to ops.jobs (PG) in auto-review-6mf.1, so the
# script no longer enumerates hosts/IPs and needs no allowlist entry.)

# Synthetic /home/mj TEST FIXTURES — explicitly out of scope per the design
# doc's "Out of scope" section (a realistic-looking but non-deployed path
# used to exercise path-parsing logic, not a leak).
agent-review/tests/test_extract_scope.py:/home/mj\b
doctor/test_doctor.py:/home/mj\b

# --- Found while wiring up this guard; not in the original 6mf.4 punch list.
# Flagged for review rather than silently narrowing the patterns above. ---

# Synthetic private IP (192.168.1.1, the canonical router-default address)
# used as DSN-redaction test input — same "test fixture" class as the two
# entries above, just not called out by name in the design doc.
agent-review/tests/test_redaction.py:192\.168\.1\.1

# Established placeholder convention: the real system name is kept as a
# human-readable label immediately beside its AUTO_REVIEW_RUNNER /
# OPENCLAW_HOST placeholder — the accepted convention this guard reuses
# rather than inventing a new style for. Not a raw, unredacted address.
AGENTS.md:openclaw
doctor/README.md:openclaw

# Retired-feature doc naming a box by role only, no address attached.
doctor/health-watch:portainer

# Timing-dependency comment naming the external push source; same class of
# leak as the doctor JOBS list above, not yet scrubbed.
scripts/run-checkin-nightly.sh:baox

# The design spec itself quoting the `.223` pattern while describing the
# remediation plan (meta-reference to the leak shape, not an instance of it).
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-27-infra-content-separation-design.md:\.223
